### Day 5/50 — Database Management System (DBMS)

Throughout life, we collect so much.

Memories,
Experiences,
Moments.

Some good.
Some bad,
Some worth keeping,
and some that we eventually learn to let go of.

Maybe, in a way we keep filtering through them—
holding on to the memories that matter,
learning from the experiences that help us,
and slowly making space for something new.

And isn't that a little like a **Database Management System**?

It's not just about having data.
It's about managing it efficiently.
Adding what is needed.
Removing what is no longer useful.
Organizing what you want to keep.

Because when everything is managed well,
making space for something new becomes easier.

** Maybe our minds work the same way....
not everything we experience has to stay forever,
but knowing what to keep, 
what to learn from 
and what to let go of... matters.**
